### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Why first |
|----------|-------|------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free | `addAndDoNothing` | 1 min | Silent false-pass — masks broken code |
| 2 | Exception Handling | `addNullSkuManualCatch` | 2 min | Broad `catch` can swallow real bugs |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `addSleepy` | 1 min | Wastes 200 ms per run, flakiness risk |
| 4 | Mystery Guest | `addLoadsFromFile` | 3 min | Filesystem dependency = CI flakiness |
| 5 | Conditional Logic | `addConditionalLogic` | 3 min | Hidden paths never verified independently |
| 6 | Eager Test | `doEverythingAtOnce` | 5 min | Split into focused tests |
| 7 | Magic Number | `quantityAfterAdds` | 2 min | Readability improvement |
| 8 | Sensitive Equality | `toStringFormat` | 2 min | Brittle to format changes |
| 9 | General Fixture | `setUp` | 1 min | Remove dead `rng` field |
| 10 | Ignored Test | `disabledTest` | 1 min | Re-enable or track properly |

Items 1–5 prevent false passes or flaky failures — fix those first. Items 6–10 are maintainability improvements.
